1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,183
AccessProof: check common
HTML accessibility gaps offline.

2
00:00:04,183 --> 00:00:08,000
A source preflight,
with human review still required.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,765
The sample shows four potential
barriers and two review prompts.

4
00:00:12,765 --> 00:00:17,000
These counts describe source
checks, not WCAG compliance.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:26,531
Each finding includes element
evidence and a repair pattern.

6
00:00:26,531 --> 00:00:38,000
A placeholder-only field is a review
prompt, not an unnamed-field error.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,600
Write the review decision
and mark the evidence reviewed.

8
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:49,000
The app keeps your local notes
with unchanged evidence.

9
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,225
Add an unnamed iframe
and rescan: one new finding appears.

10
00:00:54,225 --> 00:01:00,000
Before-and-after comparison
separates new and retained evidence.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:13,274
Source checks do not cover
computed contrast or live interaction.

12
00:01:13,274 --> 00:01:28,000
Use a rendered-page engine and test
keyboard and screen-reader behavior.

13
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:35,162
English and Chinese views share
the same local review.

14
00:01:35,162 --> 00:01:43,000
Markdown and JSON exports
preserve source and review notes.

